"It is a ten-minute walk from the Uptown Memorial ER."
"It sleeps forty women in bunk rooms, with showers and padlocked lockers."
"Doors open at five in the evening; dinner at six, lights out at ten."
"Breakfast is at six-thirty, and everyone must be out by half past seven."
"Intake asks for a name only; no ID is needed."
"No drugs, no drink and no men past the lobby; a staffer is awake all night."
"A bed the social worker reserves is held until seven; a no-show loses it."
